---
layout: layout.njk
title: "CodeSailors.dev — Rescue for AI-Built Apps & Websites"
description: "Your app was built with AI tools and now something's broken, slow, or stuck? I fix performance, debugging and maintenance issues in AI-generated codebases. Based in Brussels, working worldwide."
---

<section class="hero-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="hero-inner">
            <div class="hero-name-block">
                <h2 class="hero-name">Fix<br>my AI&nbsp;code.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-detail-block">
                <div class="hero-profile-wrap">
                    <img src="/assets/profile.jpg" alt="João Ribeiro" class="profile-image">
                </div>
                <p class="hero-role">AI-Code Rescue · Jo&atilde;o Ribeiro</p>
                <p class="hero-subtitle">You shipped fast with AI tools &mdash; Cursor, Claude, Copilot &mdash; and now something's wrong: mysterious bugs, a slow app, failing deploys, or code nobody can read. I debug, repair and harden AI-assisted apps and websites so they actually stay up.</p>
                <div class="hero-cta">
                    <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Get it fixed</a>
                    <a href="#services" class="btn btn-ghost">What I fix</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="posts-section" id="services">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="posts-header-row">
            <h2 class="section-title">What's broken? I've seen it.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="posts-grid">
            {% set issues = [
                { cat: "Slow", title: "Pages crawl, APIs lag, builds take forever", desc: "Missing indexes, N+1 queries, unoptimized bundles, no caching &mdash; I profile first, then fix what actually matters." },
                { cat: "Bugs", title: "It worked yesterday, now it doesn't", desc: "Flaky behaviour, broken auth, weird state bugs the AI can't reproduce &mdash; traced to the root cause and fixed properly." },
                { cat: "Deploy", title: "Works locally, breaks in production", desc: "Environment drift, failing builds, broken CI/CD pipelines &mdash; sorted out and made repeatable." },
                { cat: "Code", title: "Nobody can read the code anymore", desc: "Copy-pasted AI output with no structure &mdash; refactored into something a human can maintain, with tests." },
                { cat: "Stuck", title: "The AI keeps 'fixing' and making it worse", desc: "Loop of failed patches? I take over, stabilise the codebase and get you unblocked." },
                { cat: "Audit", title: "Is this thing even safe to run?", desc: "Security review of AI-generated code: exposed secrets, injection risks, broken permissions &mdash; before someone else finds them." }
            ] %}
            {% for issue in issues %}
            <article class="post-card">
                <div class="post-header">
                    <span class="post-category">{{ issue.cat }}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="post-content">
                    <h3 class="post-title">{{ issue.title }}</h3>
                    <p class="post-excerpt">{{ issue.desc }}</p>
                </div>
            </article>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="posts-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="posts-header-row">
            <h2 class="section-title">How I work</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="posts-grid">
            <article class="post-card">
                <div class="post-header">
                    <span class="post-category">Step 1</span>
                </div>
                <div class="post-content">
                    <h3 class="post-title">You describe the problem</h3>
                    <p class="post-excerpt">One form or one email. Stack, symptoms, what the AI already tried. No discovery calls required.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-footer">
                    <span class="post-time">Same-day reply</span>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="post-card">
                <div class="post-header">
                    <span class="post-category">Step 2</span>
                </div>
                <div class="post-content">
                    <h3 class="post-title">I diagnose &amp; quote</h3>
                    <p class="post-excerpt">A fixed-price diagnosis: root cause, what the fix involves, what it costs. No open-ended hourly surprises.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-footer">
                    <span class="post-time">Within 48 hours</span>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="post-card">
                <div class="post-header">
                    <span class="post-category">Step 3</span>
                </div>
                <div class="post-content">
                    <h3 class="post-title">Fixed, tested, handed over</h3>
                    <p class="post-excerpt">The fix lands in your repo with tests and a short write-up of what was wrong, so it doesn't happen again.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-footer">
                    <span class="post-time">Fixed scope &amp; price</span>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="posts-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="posts-header-row">
            <h2 class="section-title">Recent fixes</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="posts-list">
            {% if collections.posts | length > 0 %}
                {% for post in collections.posts | reverse | limit(4) %}
                <div class="post-row">
                    <span class="post-row-cat">{{ post.data.category }}</span>
                    <a href="{{ post.url }}" class="post-row-title">{{ post.data.title }}</a>
                    <span class="post-row-date">{{ post.date | dateShort }}</span>
                    <span class="post-row-arrow">&rarr;</span>
                </div>
                {% endfor %}
            {% else %}
                <p class="no-posts-message">Case studies are on the way &mdash; in the meantime, the fastest way to know if I can help is to <a href="/contact/">tell me what's broken</a>.</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="posts-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="posts-header-row">
            <h2 class="section-title">Sound like your situation?</h2>
            <a href="/contact/" class="all-posts-link">Tell me what's broken &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="posts-grid">
            <article class="post-card">
                <div class="post-content">
                    <h3 class="post-title">Free first reply</h3>
                    <p class="post-excerpt">Describe the issue and get an honest assessment &mdash; including when the answer is &ldquo;you don't need me for this&rdquo;.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-footer">
                    <span class="post-time"><a href="/contact/" class="read-more-link">Get in touch</a></span>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
